    },
    "message": "KAFKA-9998: Bound the I/O thread join in KafkaProducer.close(timeout)\n\nAfter force closing the sender, close() joined the I/O thread with no timeout, so a callback blocking that thread made close(timeout) hang forever. Cap that wait at max.block.ms and log a warning if the thread is still alive. Also stop calling Thread.join(0), which waits forever, when the close timer has already run out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
